The Debian recipe currently builds from:

  debian/config/sg2002-milkv-duo256m.config

That file is a temporary generated seed derived from:

  /root/uboot/sg2002/cv180x.riscv64.config

with the Alpine-specific localversion replaced by a Debian board suffix.

The intended long-term source of truth is:

  debian/config/base/milkv-duo_defconfig
  debian/config/fragments/debian-common.fragment
  debian/config/fragments/initramfs.fragment
  debian/config/fragments/sg2002-soc.fragment
  debian/config/fragments/sg2002-milkv-duo256m.fragment

`debian-common.fragment` should eventually be generated from the intersection
of Debian kernel configs across architectures rather than inherited from the
Alpine draft. `debian/scripts/update-config.sh` is provided for that workflow.
